// Title: Arbitrary File Download Via PresentationHost.EXE
// Sigma ID: b124ddf4-778d-418e-907f-6dd3fc0d31cd
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: 2023-11-09
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects usage of "PresentationHost" which is a utility that runs ".xbap" (Browser Applications)
//   files to download arbitrary files
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/pull/239/files
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_presentationhost_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\presentationhost.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "PresentationHost.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ftp://")
